00:27:26,979 --> 00:27:28,731
-It was insane. She was so good.
-Yeah.

495
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:29,690
So cute.

496
00:27:30,649 --> 00:27:31,650
-Oh, my God.
-Oops.

497
00:27:47,917 --> 00:27:49,168
Annie, it's me.

498
00:28:01,055 --> 00:28:02,056
Hello?

499
00:28:23,744 --> 00:28:26,747
[slow music playing]

500
00:28:44,765 --> 00:28:45,808
We're closed.

501
00:28:47,184 --> 00:28:48,519
Yeah, not here for that.

502
00:28:49,228 --> 00:28:50,563
[Joe] What are you doing here?

503
00:28:50,646 --> 00:28:52,898
Getting my kids out of here
as quickly as possible.

504
00:28:55,359 --> 00:28:56,861
So, nothing's changed.

505
00:28:56,944 --> 00:28:57,987
What'd you just say?

506
00:28:58,070 --> 00:28:59,530
I'm pretty sure you heard me.

507
00:29:03,784 --> 00:29:05,703
I heard you're not taking care of Ramona.

508
00:29:05,786 --> 00:29:07,538
Who the fuck do you think you are?

509
00:29:07,621 --> 00:29:10,166
You ruined how many lives
to not even raise her?

510
00:29:10,249 --> 00:29:13,461
How do you live with yourself, man?
What story are you telling?

511
00:29:15,421 --> 00:29:19,341
You know, the only one
telling the story here is you, pal.

512
00:29:19,425 --> 00:29:20,384
Okay.

513
00:29:21,093 --> 00:29:24,638
Well, you can tell your kid
it's not gonna work out with Annie.

514
00:29:24,722 --> 00:29:27,057
-Excuse me?
-Yeah, that's what I said.

515
00:29:27,641 --> 00:29:29,685
She won't make
the same mistakes Goldie made.

516
00:29:29,768 --> 00:29:32,813
You know exactly what happened to Goldie
and it sure as hell wasn't me.

517
00:29:32,897 --> 00:29:37,151
Yeah, you were a distraction.
This whole place is a distraction.

518
00:29:37,234 --> 00:29:38,944
It was the biggest mistake of her life.

519
00:29:39,028 --> 00:29:41,989
Or was that going to New York
to be with you?

520
00:29:42,072 --> 00:29:45,451
-Because she came back here.
-Yeah, she wasn't thinking rationally.

521
00:29:45,534 --> 00:29:48,287
You were thinking rationally
when you took her kids from her?

522
00:29:48,370 --> 00:29:49,747
She took them from me.

523
00:29:49,830 --> 00:29:53,584
You showed up in the middle of the night
with a goddamn lawyer, Steven.

524
00:29:53,667 --> 00:29:54,877
You think I wanted that?

525
00:29:57,213 --> 00:30:00,174
The fact that what happened to her
doesn't eat you up inside

526
00:30:00,257 --> 00:30:03,677
-every single day of your life…
-What the fuck do you know, man?

527
00:30:05,888 --> 00:30:08,265
Well, I know she didn't love you anymore.

528
00:30:10,142 --> 00:30:13,187
I know that she wasn't sure she ever did.

529
00:30:14,772 --> 00:30:16,398
[grunts]

530
00:30:16,482 --> 00:30:17,483
Fuck!

531
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:20,194
Goddamn it, man!

532
00:30:20,277 --> 00:30:21,570
Argh!

533
00:30:21,654 --> 00:30:22,738
See, that's what happens

534
00:30:22,821 --> 00:30:25,157
when you don't think
you're as weak as you really are.

535
00:30:33,249 --> 00:30:34,124
Fuck!

536
00:30:39,922 --> 00:30:41,674
You were so sweet with Maple today.

537
00:30:43,968 --> 00:30:45,469
No. She hated it.

538
00:30:46,136 --> 00:30:47,429
No, she didn't.

539
00:30:51,100 --> 00:30:53,978
I just didn't want her to feel
like our mum wasn't there, you know?

540
00:30:54,061 --> 00:30:56,105
Mmm.

541
00:30:56,605 --> 00:30:59,191
You were perfect, though. Really.

542
00:31:05,948 --> 00:31:07,825
I wish Annie and I would've had that.

543
00:31:09,285 --> 00:31:10,286
You will.

544
00:31:11,829 --> 00:31:14,832
You have your whole future with her.
She's not gonna go anywhere.

545
00:31:16,709 --> 00:31:17,751
Yeah.

546
00:31:19,169 --> 00:31:21,255
And I am not gonna go anywhere either.

547
00:31:22,590 --> 00:31:24,383
-So you better get used to it.
-[chuckles]

548
00:31:28,846 --> 00:31:29,680
Okay.

549
00:31:33,142 --> 00:31:34,560
I'm not going anywhere either.

550
00:31:35,102 --> 00:31:36,520
-Really?
-No.

551
00:31:36,604 --> 00:31:38,063
So you better deal with that.

552
00:31:39,815 --> 00:31:40,858
Okay.

553
00:32:06,050 --> 00:32:07,426
You're so beautiful.

554
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:29,156
Annie?

555
00:32:29,573 --> 00:32:30,491
Mmm-hmm?

556
00:32:33,327 --> 00:32:36,205
I feel like my childhood is over.

557
00:32:39,541 --> 00:32:40,376
It's not.

558
00:32:42,252 --> 00:32:43,587
I promise it's not.

559
00:32:46,548 --> 00:32:47,758
Does it get easier?

560
00:32:48,550 --> 00:32:50,761
Your period? 'Cause I still bleed

561
00:32:50,844 --> 00:32:54,223
-through my pants all the time.
-No! No, like, growing up.

562
00:32:54,306 --> 00:32:56,016
[Annie laughs] Oh. Um…

563
00:32:57,142 --> 00:32:59,520
I'm gonna be super real with you.

564
00:33:00,604 --> 00:33:01,605
No.

565
00:33:02,398 --> 00:33:03,399
[Maple] Oh.

566
00:33:03,482 --> 00:33:05,526
[chuckles] No, I'm sorry.

567
00:33:05,609 --> 00:33:08,612
I'm sorry.
I should not have said that. Uh…

568
00:33:08,696 --> 00:33:11,490
No, this is where me not having a mom
becomes scarily obvious.

569
00:33:13,450 --> 00:33:14,993
I understand why you're scared.

570
00:33:15,077 --> 00:33:17,996
It's like, growing up and changing,
and getting old, and,

571
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:21,458
like, feeling out of control,
it's really, like…

572
00:33:22,876 --> 00:33:24,253
It's really freaky.

573
00:33:26,130 --> 00:33:29,007
And please don't vomit as I say this,
but it's also kinda…

574
00:33:30,884 --> 00:33:32,678
a new chapter, right?

575
00:33:34,221 --> 00:33:36,432
Which is pretty exciting.

576
00:33:37,558 --> 00:33:41,145
What I feel right now is just,
like, weird.

577
00:33:43,021 --> 00:33:44,064
I get that.

578
00:33:47,943 --> 00:33:49,528
But it won't feel that way forever.

579
00:33:52,239 --> 00:33:55,784
[Maple] So, when does childhood end?

580
00:33:58,454 --> 00:33:59,580
[sighs]

581
00:34:06,086 --> 00:34:09,882
I guess… I guess, like, maybe
when you stop worrying that it's over?

582
00:34:44,917 --> 00:34:46,460
I'll be right back, okay?

583
00:35:13,278 --> 00:35:14,404
-Hey.
-[Ellis] Hey.

584
00:35:19,284 --> 00:35:20,285
You okay?

585
00:35:22,454 --> 00:35:23,455
Yeah.

586
00:35:25,082 --> 00:35:27,042
I just don't remember getting my period.

587
00:35:28,335 --> 00:35:29,628
Right.

588
00:35:29,711 --> 00:35:30,879
[Annie] Yeah.

589
00:35:30,963 --> 00:35:33,131
Like, it just occurred to me
how sad that is.

590
00:35:34,049 --> 00:35:35,759
I don't really remember that moment.

591
00:35:36,426 --> 00:35:37,511
Like…

592
00:35:38,637 --> 00:35:42,474
Like, I guess I went to the bodega alone
and, like, bought tampons.

593
00:35:43,058 --> 00:35:46,562
And, like, looked up on YouTube
how to put one in?

594
00:35:46,645 --> 00:35:48,897
Like, it's kinda sad.

595
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:51,942
I don't really think I had, like…

596
00:35:52,025 --> 00:35:53,610
like, experienced my childhood.

597
00:35:54,653 --> 00:35:57,614
And there's nothing anyone can do
to make me feel better about it,

598
00:35:57,698 --> 00:36:00,868
that it's over, because it's over
and I will never get it back.

599
00:36:01,827 --> 00:36:04,663
And I'm so mad at my dad for that.
I think.

600
00:36:04,746 --> 00:36:05,914
Like, like,

601
00:36:06,999 --> 00:36:11,587
why was it my responsibility to, like,
make my childhood a childhood?

602
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:14,840
Like, I feel like he took…
I took the fall for him or something.

603
00:36:14,923 --> 00:36:15,757
You know?

604
00:36:16,341 --> 00:36:20,178
I took the fall for him.
Like, I guess I couldn't be a kid,

605
00:36:20,262 --> 00:36:23,932
so that he could be sad?
Like, why did he let me do that?

606
00:36:24,016 --> 00:36:26,560
Okay, do you know what I did
on my birthday every year?

607
00:36:26,643 --> 00:36:29,187
This is really funny.
I would go to the doctor

608
00:36:29,271 --> 00:36:30,898
for my annual exam.

609
00:36:31,732 --> 00:36:34,985
'Cause I thought that that's what
you were supposed to do on your birthday.

610
00:36:36,820 --> 00:36:38,071
Who let me do that?

611
00:36:38,614 --> 00:36:40,198
And I would schedule it myself.

612
00:36:40,282 --> 00:36:42,242
No fucking wonder I hate birthdays.

613
00:36:42,326 --> 00:36:45,287
[groaning]

614
00:36:45,370 --> 00:36:47,039
Like, I wish this was a closet.

615
00:36:48,749 --> 00:36:52,628
I would… As a kid, I would, like,
go into my closet…

616
00:36:52,711 --> 00:36:54,963
It was just, like, comforting. Um…

617
00:36:55,047 --> 00:36:58,383
But is that weird to do as an adult?
To, like, sit in a closet?

618
00:36:58,926 --> 00:37:01,470
I guess I have, like, taxes to file.

619
00:37:02,137 --> 00:37:03,347
Like…

620
00:37:05,057 --> 00:37:08,769
I know everyone probably feels this way,
but I just wish I could go back

621
00:37:08,852 --> 00:37:10,020
and do it differently.

622
00:37:11,021 --> 00:37:13,023
Because then I probably
wouldn't be like this.

623
00:37:13,106 --> 00:37:15,025
And then I could just, like, be fixed.

624
00:37:17,277 --> 00:37:19,905
Oh, my God. I can't believe
I just said all that to you.

625
00:37:23,700 --> 00:37:26,870
Annie, you don't…
You don't need to be fixed, though.

626
00:37:32,584 --> 00:37:33,585
Seriously.

627
00:37:43,220 --> 00:37:46,014
Feeling hardcore enough to…

628
00:37:48,183 --> 00:37:49,559
sleep on the beach?

629
00:37:53,981 --> 00:37:55,107
Okay.

630
00:37:56,441 --> 00:37:57,526
Oh, Jesus Christ.

631
00:37:58,193 --> 00:37:59,194
-Thank you.
-Be gentle.

632
00:38:01,530 --> 00:38:04,491
Want me to call my lawyer? He's a shark.

633
00:38:04,574 --> 00:38:06,493
No, I'm fine. It's okay.

634
00:38:08,578 --> 00:38:10,414
[sighs]

635
00:38:11,581 --> 00:38:13,709
But if you can tell my kids
they're not Canadian

636
00:38:13,792 --> 00:38:16,253
and convince them to come home
with me, that'd be nice.

637
00:38:16,336 --> 00:38:20,298
Just explain how socialist taxes work.
They'll be running back to New York.

638
00:38:21,174 --> 00:38:23,135
-Yeah, that's for sure.
-Right?

639
00:38:24,594 --> 00:38:25,679
You're gonna be okay.

640
00:38:26,430 --> 00:38:27,764
Promise.

641
00:38:27,848 --> 00:38:28,849
Yeah.

642
00:38:28,932 --> 00:38:29,850
[Steven sighs]

643
00:38:30,684 --> 00:38:32,436
She's been dead a long time, honey.

644
00:38:33,020 --> 00:38:34,187
You gotta bury her.

645
00:38:42,821 --> 00:38:44,072
[sighs]

646
00:38:46,533 --> 00:38:47,868
Could you tell me a story?

647
00:38:48,827 --> 00:38:51,663
So I can ignore my impending doom
and try to fall asleep?

648
00:38:53,123 --> 00:38:54,791
Okay. Uh…

649
00:38:57,919 --> 00:38:59,463
I could…

650
00:39:00,255 --> 00:39:03,175
I could tell you how to, like,
build a canoe.

651
00:39:03,258 --> 00:39:04,551
If that's cool with you.

652
00:39:04,634 --> 00:39:06,720
-That is perfect.
-That's all I got.

653
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:08,764
[both chuckle]

654
00:39:08,847 --> 00:39:10,724
-That's exactly what I need.
-Okay.

655
00:39:10,807 --> 00:39:12,976
-I've always wondered how.
-Okay, good.

656
00:39:14,603 --> 00:39:15,771
[clears throat]

657
00:39:15,854 --> 00:39:17,481
-All right.
-Okay.

658
00:39:18,607 --> 00:39:20,025
So, um…

659
00:39:21,401 --> 00:39:24,905
I guess you start with, like,
finding the right cuts of pine, right?

660
00:39:26,073 --> 00:39:29,159
And then you have to, like,
use, like, this special tool

661
00:39:30,660 --> 00:39:33,705
to, like, shape them and curve the wood,
but you can't snap it.

662
00:39:34,956 --> 00:39:36,833
So it does take some time.

663
00:39:37,584 --> 00:39:39,211
You have to be patient with it.

664
00:39:40,545 --> 00:39:45,008
And, like, a canoe isn't
just, like, carved…

665
00:39:58,146 --> 00:39:59,606
[Joe] Where'd you find that?

666
00:40:00,232 --> 00:40:01,650
Ellis left it out.

667
00:40:02,234 --> 00:40:03,485
I'm assuming for you?

668
00:40:05,278 --> 00:40:07,864
Okay, yeah.
Why didn't you say something?

669
00:40:09,574 --> 00:40:12,702
That's the first thing you're gonna say?
Are you serious?

670
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:16,957
Were you going to leave?

671
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:20,335
I didn't leave.

672
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:21,878
That wasn't my question.

673
00:40:25,715 --> 00:40:30,303
[sighs] Were you in love with her?

674
00:40:30,387 --> 00:40:33,390
Oh, come on. This… [sighs]

675
00:40:33,473 --> 00:40:36,268
We're talking about something
that was almost 20 years ago.

676
00:40:36,351 --> 00:40:39,729
-I was young, I was confused.
-And this all happened while I was away?

677
00:40:40,438 --> 00:40:41,606
With our baby?

678
00:40:42,315 --> 00:40:44,901
Just taking care of my sick mother alone.

679
00:40:46,444 --> 00:40:48,029
-Kate, I--
-You what?

680
00:40:51,158 --> 00:40:53,910
-This is the life that I wanted.
-[scoffs]

681
00:40:55,412 --> 00:40:56,538
Oh, great.

682
00:40:57,372 --> 00:40:59,291
I'm so glad you got what you wanted.

683
00:40:59,374 --> 00:41:01,793
-That is not what I meant.
-[sighs]

684
00:41:05,422 --> 00:41:07,132
Is Ramona yours?

685
00:41:08,508 --> 00:41:10,552
-[sighs] Can we just--
-Joe.

686
00:41:11,261 --> 00:41:12,429
[sighing]

687
00:41:15,098 --> 00:41:16,099
Is she?

688
00:41:23,815 --> 00:41:25,609
And you haven't told her.

689
00:41:30,864 --> 00:41:32,324
Who are you?

690
00:41:37,078 --> 00:41:38,580
[sniffles]

691
00:41:59,976 --> 00:42:01,561
-Good morning.
-Hi.

692
00:42:08,568 --> 00:42:09,569
Made you something.

693
00:42:12,030 --> 00:42:12,864
You didn't.

694
00:42:13,448 --> 00:42:14,282
-I did.
-You…

695
00:42:16,660 --> 00:42:19,204
-Oh, I could cry right now.
-I know, but--

696
00:42:19,287 --> 00:42:20,664
I will cry in private later.

697
00:42:20,747 --> 00:42:23,708
-Thank you.
-This is… I can't believe you did this.

698
00:42:23,792 --> 00:42:24,793
Yeah. Yeah.

699
00:42:25,377 --> 00:42:26,795
Why does it look so good?

700
00:42:26,878 --> 00:42:28,004
I did props on Midsommar.

701
00:42:28,672 --> 00:42:30,423
Okay, we have a professional.

702
00:42:30,507 --> 00:42:32,008
-Yeah, no.
-Thank you for this.

703
00:42:32,509 --> 00:42:33,677
This is so cool.

704
00:42:35,595 --> 00:42:36,596
Thanks.

705
00:42:37,555 --> 00:42:40,392
Since I didn't get to make you one
when it actually happened.

706
00:42:41,309 --> 00:42:43,311
God, I wish our kid selves
got to hang out.

707
00:42:43,395 --> 00:42:45,480
-Yeah. I do, I do too.
-Right?

708
00:42:45,981 --> 00:42:47,983
I wish we could've, like,
fought each other.

709
00:42:48,066 --> 00:42:51,695
We'd be so mad at each other one second,
like, over something stupid,

710
00:42:51,778 --> 00:42:53,280
and then not care a second later.

711
00:42:53,363 --> 00:42:56,574
-Yeah. Rat each other out for stuff.
-I would never rat.

712
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:59,869
-Please.
-I would've been the worst tattletale.

713
00:42:59,953 --> 00:43:00,954
Yeah.

714
00:43:02,247 --> 00:43:03,623
This is gonna sound weird, but…

715
00:43:05,292 --> 00:43:07,419
I feel like now that I know you,
I miss her more.

716
00:43:10,088 --> 00:43:12,340
-[sighs] Yeah.
-Yeah.

717
00:43:13,842 --> 00:43:16,469
Almost felt like I didn't have the right
to be sad about it

718
00:43:16,553 --> 00:43:18,263
'cause I didn't have her to begin with.

719
00:43:19,139 --> 00:43:20,640
So, I get that.

720
00:43:22,892 --> 00:43:25,228
I sort of feel like I did have her.

721
00:43:26,313 --> 00:43:27,147
Like, as a mom.

722
00:43:29,691 --> 00:43:32,110
That she was real because I have you.

723
00:43:33,903 --> 00:43:35,697
You know, like a sister.

724
00:43:40,243 --> 00:43:44,456
[Annie chuckles softly]

725
00:43:44,539 --> 00:43:47,167
I can't believe
you just called me your sister.

726
00:43:47,876 --> 00:43:50,378
-Take it. Okay.
-I am. I love it.

727
00:43:55,884 --> 00:43:56,968
Can you say it again?

728
00:43:57,052 --> 00:43:58,636
-Okay, don't push it. Okay.
-Okay.

729
00:43:58,720 --> 00:44:05,727
["Big Wheel" playing]

730
00:44:37,050 --> 00:44:40,553
[inaudible]

731
00:44:42,138 --> 00:44:44,724
[chattering indistinctly]

732
00:44:44,808 --> 00:44:47,227
[Oona] Wait, wait, guys,
I've got the egg ick right now.

733
00:44:47,310 --> 00:44:49,229
-[Sully] Egg ick?
-Ugh, I hate the egg ick.

734
00:44:49,312 --> 00:44:51,898
I had that for, like, a year once.
It was horrible.

735
00:44:53,358 --> 00:44:54,401
Hi.

736
00:44:54,484 --> 00:44:56,027
Hey, Dad, what are you doing here?

737
00:44:56,569 --> 00:44:59,155
-Um…
-Why do you have a black eye?

738
00:44:59,239 --> 00:45:00,573
Oh, Joe kicked his ass.

739
00:45:00,657 --> 00:45:02,492
-Like, real…
-[Steven] Okay. All right.

740
00:45:02,575 --> 00:45:05,161
[Connor] Real Gen X
"when a punch is thrown" kinda thing.

741
00:45:06,746 --> 00:45:09,916
Right? Isn't it weird?
She looks just like Mom.

742
00:45:09,999 --> 00:45:12,669
Yo, what's up? I'm Ramona.
Nice to meet you.

743
00:45:13,711 --> 00:45:15,296
Dead mom's twin.

744
00:45:15,380 --> 00:45:18,341
Really appreciate you, you know,
keeping me and my siblings apart

745
00:45:18,425 --> 00:45:19,968
for our whole lives. Really cool.

746
00:45:20,051 --> 00:45:22,137
Okay. That's not… I'm sorry, but

747
00:45:22,220 --> 00:45:23,847
-what hap-- I'm sorry.
-Yeah. Yeah.

748
00:45:25,598 --> 00:45:27,517
-It's time to go.
-No, I'm not.

749
00:45:27,600 --> 00:45:29,644
Yeah. Get your stuff, please.

750
00:45:29,727 --> 00:45:32,147
I'm not leaving.
I'm the only family Ramona has.

751
00:45:32,230 --> 00:45:33,481
Steven, honey, end this now.

752
00:45:33,565 --> 00:45:36,484
-No, what?
-It's kinda getting cruel at this point.

753
00:45:36,568 --> 00:45:37,694
Denise is right, Dad.

754
00:45:38,194 --> 00:45:39,487
-Yeah. Yes.
-No. Guys, no.

755
00:45:39,571 --> 00:45:42,073
-Tell Ramona and get on with your lives.
-Enough. Not now.

756
00:45:42,157 --> 00:45:44,159
-Tell me what?
-[Steven] Don't say anything.

757
00:45:44,242 --> 00:45:45,994
Joe is your dad, Ramona.

758
00:45:46,578 --> 00:45:49,038
He is too afraid to tell you and Steven…

759
00:45:49,873 --> 00:45:52,375
It's not fair to him anymore,
or, frankly, to you, honey,

760
00:45:52,459 --> 00:45:54,961
and I'm so sorry
that you had to find out like this.

761
00:45:57,464 --> 00:46:00,008
-There, I've said it. Now it's done.
-Jesus Christ, Denise.

762
00:46:03,553 --> 00:46:04,429
You two knew?

763
00:46:07,807 --> 00:46:08,808
Joe knows?

764
00:46:11,478 --> 00:46:12,520
Say something.

765
00:46:14,189 --> 00:46:16,774
Gordon made him your guardian
when he died.

766
00:46:20,445 --> 00:46:22,113
-Ramona, I--
-Annie, you said…

767
00:46:26,201 --> 00:46:28,828
You said, "No more secrets."

768
00:46:30,330 --> 00:46:32,957
-No, I know--
-Ramona. Hey, Ramona, wait.

769
00:46:33,041 --> 00:46:34,042
[Sully] Ramona.

770
00:46:35,877 --> 00:46:37,879
["White Horses" playing]

771
00:46:37,962 --> 00:46:40,173
Actually, fuck all of you.

772
00:46:41,674 --> 00:46:43,259
Fuck you.

773
00:46:43,343 --> 00:46:44,427
[Annie] Oona, I…

774
00:46:54,687 --> 00:46:55,688
Wait!

775
00:46:56,606 --> 00:46:57,607
Ramona!

